{
  "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
  "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nANDREW R. HINKEL, Assistant State Public Defender, Madison, Wisconsin; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nHANNAH S. JURSS, Assistant Attorney General, Madison, Wisconsin; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew R. Hinkel (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State advances a bold and novel proposition here, that it can excuse itself from the Fourth Amendment warrant requirement simply by enacting a statute saying that some of its -- that its citizens have consented to a search."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is it -- it doesn't strike me immediately as that horrendous to allow the officers to look, not through the cell phone, but to sort of calls, find out was this person calling somebody or talking to somebody at the time they, you know, ran over somebody else? Is that -- is that so obviously --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Don't you have an -- an unconstitutional conditions argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Jurss",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. JURSS: So this Court could decide it under one of two theories: either consent or as a condition of driving, which would fall under a general reasonableness balancing test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Jurss",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. JURSS: Yes, it's a special application of consent, but it still is consent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: How is it consent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But we normally -- we normally take state law as it's given to us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But is there a way --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do we remand for -- I mean, you know, there's certification and all, which is -- I don't say usually but often doesn't quite work out the way you hope."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. JURSS",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We would agree. And we agree that there -- we assert that there is enough here for this Court to decide based on the Wisconsin Supreme Court's rationale."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In some of these situations, I assume it'll be a single officer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That sounds like an exigent circumstance argument, which you stipulated against in seeking --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why -- why do you -- the problem I'm having with your argument is I don't know where you get the implied consent from."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew R. Hinkel",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has repeatedly recognized that a blood draw is a significant interest that affects -- sorry, that offends an individual's sense of dignity and bodily integrity. And, ordinarily, this is true whether or not the person is conscious."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Didn't we just hear some reasons why the warrant would -- would -- the warrant requirement would create problems?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what's on the other side of the balance where you have somebody who's unconscious, so will not even be able to perceive that the blood test is being administered, and the person is in all likelihood having a blood draw for other purposes anyway?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the problem that the Fourth Amendment seeks to protect against is the invasion of privacy. That's the same. The interest that this Court identified in Birchfield, the anxiety that comes along with knowing that the government is in possession of this information about you, that's the same"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "How many --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So -- I mean, in Birchfield, you say I'm going to take your license away unless you're going to agree. I mean, of course, he's going to agree. So -- so that's ridiculous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, no, you're right, not every case, but on many it'll be confusing and a few he'll say no, but 99 percent, sure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-6210",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8a27575c0d502cc2b04612dd129b92b14dd0afe5a373446c46810fbeb3734a71",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8a27575c0d50-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 2:01 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
